&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the technical infrastructure that powers Cloudflare’s Go-To-Market (GTM) engine. You will develop AI-powered agents and web applications to automate and scale core marketing and sales functions. This role is for a high-agency engineer who wants to use a modern full-stack approach to solve real-world business bottlenecks, bridging the gap between strategic GTM needs and technical execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get out of this internship:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generative AI &amp;amp; Agents:&lt;/strong&gt; Master the Cloudflare Agents SDK and LLM orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Stack Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Build scalable, stateful GTM applications at the Edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn how technology directly enables global sales and marketing success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entrepreneurship:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the lifecycle of a technical project from ideation to internal launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Translation:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn to communicate the business impact of technical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering GTM Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and deploy production-ready agents using the Cloudflare stack (Workers, Agents SDK, Sandbox SDK, Durable Objects etc..).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Design autonomous workflows using Workers AI and Vectorize (RAG) to automate technical Case Studies, Sales Enablement, and Event Messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rapid Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Windsurf, or OpenCode) to move from concept to a shipped internal tool in weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Sales/Marketing to identify gaps, then build, launch, and manage the internal lifecycle of your technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Requirements (Must-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or program in CS or Engineering with a focus on building functional systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to commit to a minimum 12 week summer internship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In office 3-5 days a week in Austin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in TypeScript/JavaScript, React, and Tailwind CSS, with experience building/consuming RESTful APIs and working with SQL or NoSQL databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Git/GitHub and hands-on experience with AI coding environments (Claude Code, Windsurf, or OpenCode).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter capable of taking a technical requirement from 0 to 1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Have Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloudflare Native:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience having built and deployed projects on the &lt;strong&gt;Cloudflare Developer Platform&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Previous experience in a startup environment or building your own independent projects &quot;in public.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
