&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Department&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Sales organization—comprising Account Executives, Partner Sales Managers, Solutions Engineers, and Customer Success—operates as a cohesive ecosystem dedicated to helping the world’s most sophisticated organizations adopt Cloudflare. We don’t just sell products; we solve the internet’s most complex technical challenges. By driving revenue through high-stakes enterprise partnerships, our team enables Cloudflare to provide free, secure services to millions of users worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role: Senior Majors Account Executive (Suisse Romande)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Majors Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be the strategic lead for Cloudflare’s most significant opportunities within the &lt;strong&gt;Suisse Romande&lt;/strong&gt; region. You are responsible for penetrating and expanding our footprint within the French-speaking Suisse Romande largest multinational headquarters, and high-growth innovators like Nestle, PMI or MSC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;&quot;Hunter&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; role at its core, requiring a sophisticated approach to account planning, C-level relationship mapping, and the execution of complex sales cycles. You will act as the &quot;CEO of your territory,&quot; orchestrating internal resources to deliver transformative value to the region’s most prestigious organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Territory Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute a comprehensive sales strategy for the Suisse Romande region, focusing on a curated list of high-value &quot;Major&quot; accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Deal Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead multi-stakeholder sales campaigns, moving beyond transactional selling to deliver holistic, $1M+ ARR transformations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain deep-rooted relationships with CISOs, CTOs, and CIOs within the G2000, Swiss SMI, and private banking/pharma sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline &amp;amp; Forecast Accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a disciplined and transparent sales pipeline, ensuring accurate forecasting and consistent over-achievement of revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ecosystem Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the Channel/Alliances team to leverage local partners and integrators to scale your reach within the Swiss market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Network:&lt;/strong&gt; A robust, existing network of decision-makers within the &lt;strong&gt;Suisse Romande Enterprise&lt;/strong&gt; landscape, particularly in &lt;strong&gt;Consumer Goods, Financial Services, and Luxury/Manufacturing &lt;/strong&gt;is a must.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Experience of large multi-million dollar transformation projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linguistic Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Native or bilingual proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;French&lt;/strong&gt; and professional fluency in &lt;strong&gt;English&lt;/strong&gt; are mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of direct B2B sales experience, with a minimum of &lt;strong&gt;5+ years specifically managing Major/Strategic accounts&lt;/strong&gt; in Switzerland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Domain Authority:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record selling complex SaaS, Cybersecurity (Zero Trust), Cloud Infrastructure, or Edge Computing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Methodology:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep experience in structured sales methodologies (e.g., MEDDIC, Force Management, Challenger) to navigate long, complex procurement cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entrepreneurial Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience as an early-stage contributor for a US-based SaaS company in the Swiss market is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Must be based in the &lt;strong&gt;Suisse Romande Region&lt;/strong&gt;, with the mobility and willingness to travel extensively within the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Aptitude&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to articulate &quot;how the internet works&quot; and translate complex networking concepts into business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Academic Background:&lt;/strong&gt; BA/BS degree required; a degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or an MBA is a significant advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Thrives in a high-growth, fast-paced environment where change is the only constant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
